# insta writes these when a snapshot assertion fails; they are the rejected
# candidate, reviewed with `cargo insta review` and never committed.
*.snap.new

# `connector-nfs` is its own workspace root (see its Cargo.toml), so cargo
# writes a lockfile beside it. It is a library, and its resolution is already
# pinned by the workspace lock it is built alongside, so committing a second one
# would only give it something to drift from.
/crates/data-connectors/connector-nfs/Cargo.lock
